>
    <p>For most small businesses, the lease or the building is the largest commitment they will ever sign. Commercial property law gives the parties a great deal of freedom, which means the documents matter more than the default rules do: the lease or the purchase contract is, very nearly, the whole of the law between you.</p>
    <p>We read those documents line by line, alongside the title commitment, the survey and the county’s zoning map, and we keep a calendar of every deadline from the day you sign. Many of the problems we are asked to solve later were visible in the paperwork on the first day.</p>
